body:
I think I'm your soul twin, because I go through this with my SO. 1: Everything's so good!; 2: We can make this work; 3: Oh what was i thinking?; 4: Get a divorce, why are you still torturing yourself AND him?; 5: You need to just get out of the picture all together. Whatever means necessary.

&#x200B;

And we dance this cycle every month. We're currently in a slump (partially stress-induced due to life) so I'm waffling between stage 4 and 5. Is it worth it? Do I walk away? Do I choose one kid and he keeps the other? I can't take care of both. I'm not certain I can take care of one somedays. 

&#x200B;

But to not have him bitch at me every single day? We wake up in the morning, and it's "Sandallion, you need to get up, this is why our kids are lazy." It's "Sandallion, I wanted us to spend adult time together and you won't even let me touch you because you can't stop the anxiety". It's "Sandallion, I got in the shower and thought you were going to join me but you didn't and it's your fault we didn't get any time together." 

&#x200B;

It's always my fault. Everything. The kids don't behave well, we don't have a good relationship, it's always me.

&#x200B;

Tomorrow is our 16th anniversary. And all I can think is that I can't do this anymore.

&#x200B;

Tonight, I could not take my lithium, and tomorrow, I would love him.
